{
  "requirement": "For requirement and example evidence, both `true` and `FIXME` MUST satisfy the determination check in `habeas::validate()`. A false determination MUST fail validation and be reported with its rationale. Each definition's determination MUST be checked on its own; a false determination MUST NOT fail the definitions it implements, tests, or cites. All other evidence checks MUST still pass: FIXME MUST NOT excuse malformed, missing, or stale evidence or uncovered references. Validation MUST check the recorded outcome, schema, input freshness, and reference coverage without inference or reassessing whether a source comment adequately acknowledges a gap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: true.** The code implements every obligation of `requirements.ci.determination`, the marking is complete, and the tests cover the main cases.\n\n**Implementation** (`src/evidence.rs`, `validate_evidence_file`, marked `{impl}` at about line 644):\n- The determination is parsed with `Judgment::from_value` (`src/judgment.rs`). It accepts `true`, `false` and `{\"FIXME\": [nonempty strings]}`, and reports anything else as a schema error.\n- Only `Judgment::False` pushes an error. The error is `\"<label>: determination is false: <trimmed rationale>\"`, so a false determination fails validation and is reported with its rationale. `true` and `FIXME` add no determination error.\n- The check runs inside the per-file function, once per evidence record. A false record yields an error only for its own file, so it does not fail the definitions it implements, tests or cites.\n- FIXME is not special-cased anywhere in the other checks, so FIXME cannot excuse the rest of validation:\n  - Schema checks still run: key set, text field, rationale, and malformed or missing determination.\n  - Requirement-text freshness still runs.\n  - Input freshness still runs, via `validate_input` and the outline hash checks.\n  - Dependencies and reference coverage (`validate_references`, \"no input covers\") still run.\n  - No code reassesses whether a source comment adequately acknowledges a gap. The FIXME entries are only schema-validated for being nonempty strings.\n- The one place that looks at the determination outside this requirement is the check that a true example has a `{test}` reference. It is a separate requirement and uses `as_bool == Some(true)`.\n- I found no other code that implements this requirement without an `{impl}` marker. `src/index.rs` and `src/judgment.rs` only consume or cite the outcome and are marked for other requirements.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `a_false_determination_fails_only_its_own_record_with_its_rationale` checks the exact error string, including trimmed rationale. It also checks that the true record the false one implements and cites is unaffected.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks that a false record reports \"determination is false\" together with other errors, and that missing determination and other malformed fields are still reported.\n- `tests/outcomes.rs`:\n  - `fixme_requirements_accept_issue_references_and_other_content` shows FIXME passes, both with an issue number and with free text.\n  - `fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not` shows FIXME passes and false fails.\n  - `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` shows FIXME does not excuse stale inputs or uncovered `{impl}` references.\n- `tests/commands.rs` (`fixme_fixture`) validates FIXME records with varied entries for both requirements and examples.\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs` shows validation passing with a FIXME record, and shows false judgments being preserved and then reauthored once their inputs go stale.\n\n**Remaining gap:** no test writes a FIXME record with a malformed field and asserts that the error still appears. The FIXME-specific tests cover stale inputs and uncovered references, and the schema tests use true and false records. Because the code has no FIXME-specific branch, I don't count this as a real gap.\n\nThere are no FIXME acknowledgements for this requirement.",
  "inputs": [
